{
  "_about": "Approximate world population by year for the globe's population readout (Day 67). Values are Our World in Data's long-run 'Population' series, rounded to 4 significant figures: HYDE 3.3 (2023) for 10,000 BCE to 1799, Gapminder v7 (2022) for 1800 to 1949, UN World Population Prospects 2024 for 1950 on (2024 onward are the UN medium-variant figures). The site interpolates log-linearly between points. Pre-1800 figures are uncertain by tens of percent (1 CE estimates run from about 170 to 330 million; 10,000 BCE from about 1 to 10 million); treat them as orders of magnitude. HYDE's year '0' is stored as 1 CE.",
